From 9e25586d85599a7c72ffc01bf535d5ce542cfb3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 01:52:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] SMC: stop write-protecting pages that keep faulting,
 verify their code in the JIT instead

With SMCChecks=mtrack a page that mixes code with data that is written all the time (trampoline pools, JIT heaps,
anti-cheat hook pages) takes a SIGSEGV, an invalidation and a re-translation for every write.

Count SMC write faults per guest page (lock-free table, every mirror of a shared mapping is counted so the executed
mirror is the one that gets flagged). After SMCHotPageFaults faults (default 32, 0 disables) the page is left
writable and the JIT emits the SMCChecks=full per-instruction CRC check for instructions translated from it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
